    "title": "pandas.Series.cat.remove_unused_categories — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.cat.remove_unused_categories#\n\n- \nSeries.cat.remove_unused_categories(**args* ,***kwargs* )[source]#\n- Remove categories which are not used. \n  - Returns\n    - Categorical\n    - Categorical with unused categories dropped.\n See also \n  - `rename_categories`\n  - Rename categories.\n  - `reorder_categories`\n  - Reorder categories.\n  - `add_categories`\n  - Add new categories.\n  - `remove_categories`\n  - Remove the specified categories.\n  - `set_categories`\n  - Set the categories to the specified ones.\n Examples >>> c = pd.Categorical(['a', 'c', 'b', 'c', 'd']) >>> c ['a', 'c', 'b', 'c', 'd'] Categories (4, object): ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'] >>> c[2] = 'a' >>> c[4] = 'c' >>> c ['a', 'c', 'a', 'c', 'c'] Categories (4, object): ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'] >>> c.remove_unused_categories() ['a', 'c', 'a', 'c', 'c'] Categories (2, object): ['a', 'c']",
    "markdown_length": 855,
